stitis: less likely due to young age and lack of typical risk factors (e.g., gallstones)", "Alcoholic pancreatitis: inconsistent with RUQ localization and acute shock presentation", "Appendicitis: atypical for shock and localized RUQ pain without migratory pattern", "Ruptured ovarian cyst (non-gestational): considered but ranked lower than ectopic pregnancy due to β-hCG testing priority"], "alarm_features": ["Hypotension and tachycardia (shock)", "Sexual activity without contraception", "Recent significant weight loss", "History of gonococcal urethritis (potential pelvic pathology)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Gynecological Emergency with Hemorrhage", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.4639175257731959, "posterior": 0.3693790149892935, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The shock and RUQ pain during exercise provide weak evidence for a gynecological hemorrhage (B1), but the absence of classic ectopic pregnancy symptoms (e.g., …"], "evidence_against": ["The lack of missed period weakly reduces the probability of ectopic pregnancy (B1), but sexual activity without contraception maintains suspicion."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Biliary Tract Obstruction", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.193, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The RUQ pain without jaundice or fever moderately reduces the likelihood of B2."]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Hepatic Vascular Insufficiency", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.074, "danger": 0.8, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The acute shock presentation 